--- title Finding with refinements
--- about FIND has nine refinements and they combine, so what is pinned
--- about here is what each one changes rather than that finding works.
--- about The two below are the ones whose rule is not guessable.

--- id finding/a-block-needle-is-a-sequence-not-a-value
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The thing to know before any of the rest. FIND given a block
--- note looks for that run of items inside the series, so
--- note `find [1 2 3] [2 3]` succeeds and `find [[1]] [1]` does not --
--- note the second is asking for a bare 1.
--- code
mold find [1 2 3] [2 3]
--- result
"[2 3]"

--- id finding/a-block-needle-does-not-match-a-nested-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: reduce [[1] "x"]
find b [1]
--- result
_

--- id finding/only-makes-the-needle-one-value
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note And this is what /only is for: stop reading the block as a run
--- note and look for the block itself.
--- code
b: reduce [[1] "x"]
index? find/only b [1]
--- result
1

--- id finding/equality-takes-the-first-equal-one
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
a: [1]
d: reduce ["x" [1] a]
index? find/only d [1]
--- result
2

--- id finding/identity-passes-over-the-merely-equal
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note /same asks whether it is the same value rather than an equal
--- note one, so it walks past the block at position 2 and finds the
--- note one that actually is A.
--- code
a: [1]
d: reduce ["x" [1] a]
index? find/only/same d a
--- result
3

--- id finding/records-only-match-at-a-boundary
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note /skip reads the series as fixed-width records, so a match that
--- note starts halfway through one does not count. Here the tag sits
--- note at position 2 of a two-wide record and is missed.
--- code
find/skip "a<a>b" <a> 2
--- result
_

--- id finding/a-record-boundary-that-does-line-up
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
find/skip "aa<a>b" <a> 2
--- result
"<a>b"

--- id finding/skipping-through-a-block-of-records
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold find/skip [1 2 3 4] 3 2
--- result
"[3 4]"

--- id finding/a-value-that-is-never-at-a-boundary
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
find/skip [1 2 3 4] 2 2
--- result
_
